# Build output
bin/
dist/

# Go binaries. The Windows target is apiproxy.exe; the anchored /apiproxy
# catches a stray `go build ./cmd/apiproxy` in the module root, which writes
# a binary named after the package. It must stay anchored with the leading
# slash: an unanchored `apiproxy` would match the cmd/apiproxy/ directory and
# silently ignore the entire CLI.
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/apiproxy

# Go test and coverage artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
cover.html

# Go workspace files. These are per-developer and pin local module paths,
# so they must not be shared.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Secrets. None of these belong in the repo, and this tool exists precisely
# to keep credentials out of places an agent can read. The real config lives
# in %AppData% and the encrypted token blobs in %LocalAppData%, both outside
# the repo, but ignore local copies in case someone drops one here while
# testing.
*.env
.env
.env.*
config.toml
config.local.toml
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
